    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Aga Khan University (AKU) will hold a two-day Symposium on Infectious Diseases on September 20 and September 21, 1999, which will be followed by a Molecular Biology Workshop on infectious disease from September 22-26. The major focus of the symposium will be infectious diseases of national relevance, such as tuberculosis, hepatitis, malaria and typhoid. In 1990, the worldwide estimates of deaths over the age of five resulting from these diseases were: 1.9 million for tuberculosis, 0.3 million for malaria and 2 million for other tropical diseases. Pakistan is among the top ten countries for deaths from these diseases. Tuberculosis was among the two major causes of deaths in women in 1990. These figures have risen dramatically in the last decade.",
